    "message": "fix(php): resolve nullable types and plain-function parameters\n\nThe receiver-type queries matched `named_type` only. `?Service` is not one --\ntree-sitter-php wraps it as `(optional_type (named_type (name)))` -- so every\nnullable dependency fell back to a bare method name. In modern PHP that is most\nof them, which made the feature miss the common case rather than an edge one.\n\nSame shape in the parameter query, rooted at `method_declaration`: a top-level\n`function run(Service $svc)` is a `function_definition`, a different node, so\nits parameters were never typed at all.\n\nBoth fixed by accepting `optional_type` alongside `named_type` and alternating\nthe parameter pattern over both declaration nodes. No handler change was needed\n-- `childForFieldName('name')` works on `function_definition`, and with no\nenclosing class the scope becomes the bare function name, which is what\n`findEnclosingFunction` already returns for one.\n\nUnion types are deliberately still bare: a union has no single receiver type to\nattribute the call to, so an arbitrary pick of one member would be worse than\nthe honest fallback. Pinned with a test so it reads as intent, not omission.\n\nThree regression tests; the two for the fixed gaps fail without this change.",
